{{also|Klick}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{homophones|lang=en|click|clique}}

===Etymology 1===
* Most likely a pseudo-condensed pronunciation of {{m|en|kilometer}}.
* Possibly onomatopoeic of the sound of a military odometer.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|slang|military}} A [[kilometer]].
#* '''2002''', [[w:Robert J. Sawyer|Robert J. Sawyer]], ''Hominids''
#*: an asteroid between one and three kilometers wide had slammed into the ground at fifteen '''klicks''' per second.
# {{lb|en|slang|usually plural}} [[kilometre|Kilometres]] per [[hour]].

=====Usage notes=====
Though kilometers are not commonly used to measure distance in the USA, {{m|en||klick}} is commonly used by the US military, which uses the metric system almost exclusively in order to facilitate communication with allied forces. (In other English-speaking countries, civilians often say "k" or "k.m." instead.)

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|military slang: kilometer}} {{l|en|click}}

